        {
          "title": "Branching, Loops and Match",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Branching and loops",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`if/elif/else` runs the ==first true branch== only",
                "Conditional expression: `a if cond else b`",
                "`for` iterates ==any iterable==",
                "`range(start, stop, step)` ==excludes stop==",
                "`enumerate(xs, start=1)` and `zip(a, b)` replace index juggling"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Loop else",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`for`/`while` `else` runs only if the loop ended ==without break==",
                "Skipped on `break`; runs on ==zero iterations=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "for n in [3, 5]:",
                "    if n == 4:",
                "        break",
                "else:",
                "    print('no 4')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "no 4"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. match patterns",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Syntax"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Literal",
                  "`case 404`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sequence",
                  "`case [x, y]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Mapping",
                  "`case {'k': v}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Class",
                  "`case Point(x=0)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Or",
                  "`case A | B`"
                ],
                [
                  "Guard",
                  "`case n if n > 0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Wildcard",
                  "`case _`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Bare name captures",
              "text": "`case RED` matches anything and ==binds== RED. Use a dotted name like `Color.RED` to ==compare== against a constant."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comprehensions and Generators",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Comprehensions and Generators",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Comprehension Forms",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Syntax"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "List",
                  "`[f(x) for x in xs if cond]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Dict",
                  "`{k: v for ...}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Set",
                  "`{x for ...}`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Filter goes ==last==: `[x for x in xs if c]`",
                "Conditional expression goes ==before `for`==: `[a if c else b for x in xs]`",
                "Nested loops read ==left to right==, same order as the for statements"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]",
                "print([x for row in m for x in row])"
              ],
              "note": "outer loop first, inner loop second"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lazy and Scoped",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`(x for x in xs)` is ==lazy== and **single-use**",
                "`sum(x*x for x in xs)` needs ==no extra brackets==",
                "The comprehension variable stays ==local==; a for-loop variable **leaks**"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Plain Loop Instead",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Body has ==side effects==",
                "Needs more than ==two clauses=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Build a value",
              "text": "A comprehension is for ==building a value==. If you ignore the result, write a loop."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Operators and Truthiness",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Operators and Truthiness",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Truthiness",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Falsy}: `None` `False` `0` `0.0` `''` `[]` `{}` `()` `set()` `range(0)`",
                "==Everything else== is truthy",
                "Custom class: `__bool__` first, then `__len__`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. and / or",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both return an ==operand==, not a bool",
                "`x or 'default'` gives the **first truthy** value",
                "`a and b` gives the **first falsy** value, else the last",
                "Both ==short-circuit==: the rest is never evaluated"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compare and Arithmetic",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operator",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`==` / `is`",
                  "value / ==identity==; use `is None`"
                ],
                [
                  "`1 < x <= 10`",
                  "chained, x evaluated **once**"
                ],
                [
                  "`//`",
                  "floors toward {red:negative infinity}"
                ],
                [
                  "`%`",
                  "takes the **divisor's** sign"
                ],
                [
                  "`in`",
                  "O(1) set/dict, O(n) list"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "print('' or 'default', 3 and 0, -7 // 2, 7 % -2)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "default 0 -4 -1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Walrus `if (n := len(xs)) > 3:` assigns inside an expression"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never",
              "text": "`is 0` or `is 'a'` is a bug. Use `==`; reserve `is` for `None`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
