              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. str vs bytes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`str` = ==Unicode code points==; `bytes` = raw 8-bit values",
                "`s.encode('utf-8')` gives bytes; `b.decode('utf-8')` gives str",
                "They never mix: `'a' + b'a'` raises {red:TypeError}",
                "UTF-8 uses ==1 to 4 bytes== per character and is ASCII-compatible"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "print(len('é'), len('é'.encode()))"
              ],
              "note": "1 character, 2 bytes"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1 2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Files and errors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The default encoding depends on the ==platform==",
                "Always pass `encoding='utf-8'` to `open()`, `.encode()`, `.decode()`",
                "Binary files: mode `'rb'`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "errors=",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'strict'` (default)",
                  "raises UnicodeDecodeError / UnicodeEncodeError"
                ],
                [
                  "`'replace'`, `'ignore'`",
                  "{red:hides bad data}"
                ],
                [
                  "`'backslashreplace'`",
                  "shows escapes, good for debugging"
