          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Code: `for n in [2, 4, 5]:` with body `if n % 2: break`, then a loop `else: print('all even')`. What prints?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Nothing.",
                "5 is odd, so `break` fires and the loop `else` is skipped."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Code: `match c:` with `case RED:` then `case _:`, where RED is a constant. What happens, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Python raises SyntaxError when it compiles the code, so nothing prints.",
                "Bare `RED` is a capture, not a comparison. It would match anything, which makes `case _` unreachable, so the compiler rejects it.",
                "Fix: write `case Color.RED:`, a dotted name, to compare."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Code: `print(0 or 'x', 'y' and 0)`. What prints?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`x 0`",
                "`or` returns the first truthy operand, `x`.",
                "`and` returns the first falsy operand, `0`."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
